   "voice": "en-US-AvaNeural",
   "text": "The Boss of Nvidia Quits.\nJensen Huang started the chip company Nvidia in 1993.\nNvidia makes the computer chips that power AI.\nUnder his leadership, it became one of the most valuable companies in the world.\nOn October 29, The New York Times wrote a story about a woman named Alice Huang.\nShe is a business executive.\nShe is not related to Jensen Huang.\nAmerican officials reportedly think she may be a spy for China.\nOn November 8, Jensen Huang wrote a letter to Nvidia's workers.\nHe said he had a relationship with her while he was married.\nHe said he was very sorry.\nNvidia's board started an investigation.\nMany people were worried.\nNvidia's chips are very important to the United States.\nIf a spy got close to the boss, could she learn secrets?\nNvidia said it had no reason to believe that any secrets were lost.\nOn November 12, Jensen Huang quit his job.\nHe was the boss of Nvidia for thirty-three years.\nColette Kress, the head of the company's money, is now the temporary boss.\nNvidia's stock price went down that day."
